# RDI YAML Conformance Checklist

Before changing any file under `rdi/`, confirm the change exists in the
official Redis docs. If a key, block, function, or data type is not
documented, do not use it.

## `rdi/config.yaml` checklist

Schema: <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/config-yaml-reference/>

- `sources.<id>.type` ∈ `cdc | external | flink | riotx`
- `sources.<id>.connection.type` ∈ `mariadb | mysql | oracle | postgresql | sqlserver` (or `mongodb`, `spanner`, `snowflake` with their own connection schemas)
- `sources.<id>.advanced.source.*` — must be a Debezium connector property (omit `debezium.source.` prefix)
- `sources.<id>.advanced.sink.*` — must be a [Debezium Redis stream sink](https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/operations/debezium-server.html#_redis_stream) property (omit `debezium.sink.` prefix)
- `processors.*` — only spec-current keys; remove anything marked **DEPRECATED**
- Secret references must use the documented names: `SOURCE_DB_USERNAME`, `SOURCE_DB_PASSWORD`, `TARGET_DB_USERNAME`, `TARGET_DB_PASSWORD`, plus the TLS variants

Known deprecated keys — never re-introduce:

- `processors.duration` → use `read_batch_timeout_ms`
- `processors.on_failed_retry_interval` → remove (no effect)
- `processors.dedup_strategy` → remove (only `ignore` supported)

## `rdi/jobs/*.yaml` checklist

Schema: <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/data-pipelines/transform-examples/>

- `source.{server_name, db, schema, table, row_format, case_insensitive}` — only these keys
- `transform[].uses` must be a documented block from <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/data-transformation/>:
  `filter`, `rename_field`, `add_field`, `remove_field`, `add_field_to_object`, `merge_fields`, …
- `transform[].with.language` ∈ `jmespath | sql`
- `output[].uses` = `redis.write` (only allowed value)
- `output[].with.data_type` ∈ `hash | json | set | sorted_set | stream | string`
- `output[].with.key.language` ∈ `jmespath | sql`
- JMESPath functions in expressions must be in
  <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/jmespath-custom-functions/>
  or [JMESPath builtins](https://jmespath.org/proposals/functions.html)

## After editing

1. Update `docs/05-rdi-spec-conformance.md` if you added new constructs.
2. If the reference processor in `rdi-processor/processor.py` does not
   yet implement the construct, either add support or revert the YAML.
3. Restart the processor: `docker compose restart rdi-processor`.
4. Re-run `./scripts/verify-redis-enterprise.sh` and confirm all checks pass.
